fi, priser, videoer hos SlowBlues.', 'MY BABY är ett nederländsk-nyzeeländskt band från Amsterdam som blandar deltablues-trance med funk och soul. Biografi, priser, videor hos SlowBlues.', 'MY BABY ist eine niederländisch-neuseeländische Band aus Amsterdam, die Delta-Blues-Trance mit Funk und Soul verbindet. Biografie, Auszeichnungen, Videos bei SlowBlues.', 'MY BABY to holendersko-nowozelandzki zespół z Amsterdamu łączący transowy delta blues z funkiem i soulem. Biografia, nagrody, wideo na SlowBlues.', '{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/mybabywashere/","facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/MYBABYMUSIC"}', '[{"label":"Bandcamp","url":"https://mybaby.bandcamp.com/"}]', '[{"title":"en.wikipedia.org — MY BABY","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Baby_(band)"},{"title":"MusicBrainz — MY BABY","url":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/d88c38de-ca0b-454a-a493-8c1494b67c27"}]', 'https://www.mybabywashere.com/', 'https://www.facebook.com/MYBABYMUSIC', '{"booking_agency":"MOJO (Nederland)","agent_name":"Jarn van Strijen","booking_email":"J.van.Strijen@mojo.nl","booking_phone":null,"booking_url":"https://www.mybabywashere.com/contact","source_url":"https://www.mybabywashere.com/contact","note":"Verifisert via bandets offisielle kontaktside. Management: Fred van Kruining (Meet Me There Management, fred@67mgmt.com, +31 6 10 33 28 16)."}', '[]');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO artists (id, slug, name, alt_name, tag, era, region, country, base_path, img, og_image, image_credit, gallery_images, youtube_video_ids, short_en, short_no, short_sv, short_de, short_pl, biography_en, biography_no, biography_sv, biography_de, biography_pl, born, died, birth_name, birth_place, origin, active_years, influence_en, influence_no, influence_sv, influence_de, influence_pl, bio, signature_songs_i18n, labels, instruments_simple, styles, family_i18n, formative_i18n, instruments_i18n, anecdotes_i18n, collaborators_i18n, videos, discography_i18n, key_recordings, awards_i18n, press_quotes_i18n, seo_title_en, seo_title_no, seo_title_sv, seo_title_de, seo_title_pl, seo_description_en, seo_description_no, seo_description_sv, seo_description_de, seo_description_pl, social_links, external_links, article_references, website_url, facebook_url, booking_info, related_slugs) VALUES ('f1a2b3c4-4444-4a6e-9c8b-2d1e5f7a9b3c', 'hans-theessink', 'Hans Theessink', NULL, 'Modern', 'Modern Era', 'Western Europe', 'Netherlands', '/artists', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/Vienna_2012-02-21_Konzerthaus_Blues%2BBoogie_Event_-_Hans_Theessink_sequence.jpg', NULL, 'Foto: Wolfgang H. Wögerer (Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0)', '[]', '["P951k311Cek","xECo-emMYnI","pUBWb2fzzZQ","G9K4P4xiU5Y","fGLH3V4CKT8","Pdh_TNefhWE","UUvQzYnz-3M","xwWRXqF0E1Q","Sgu9n5IUvCM"]', 'A Dutch-born, Vienna-based acoustic country-blues master with a career spanning over five decades.', 'En nederlandskfødt, Wien-basert akustisk country-blues-mester med en karriere som strekker seg over fem tiår.', 'En nederländskfödd, Wienbaserad akustisk country-blues-mästare med en karriär som sträcker sig över fem decennier.', 'Ein in den Niederlanden geborener, in Wien lebender Meister des akustischen Country-Blues mit einer über fünf Jahrzehnte langen Karriere.', 'Urodzony w Holandii, mieszkający w Wiedniu mistrz akustycznego country bluesa z karierą trwającą ponad pięć dekad.', 'Hans Theessink was born on 5 April 1948 in Enschede, the Netherlands, and has become one of Europe''s most respected acoustic country-blues artists (Source: de.wikipedia.org; en.wikipedia.org). Self-taught on guitar after hearing recordings of Big Bill Broonzy and Lead Belly in the early 1960s, he also picked up mandolin and banjo, and began his performing life as a street musician with the Silly Skiffle Group across the Netherlands and Germany. After a spell in Denmark, where he recorded his 1970 debut album "Next Morning at Sunrise," he relocated permanently to Vienna, Austria in 1982, following a 1979 concert where he met his future wife Milica Djokic, who has managed his career ever since through their own label and agency, Blue Groove (Source: de.wikipedia.org). Theessink''s music draws on Delta blues, folk, gospel, soul, Cajun, New Orleans jazz and African traditions, played almost entirely on acoustic instruments without digital effects. Since 2004 he has toured with the Hans Theessink Band, and has worked closely with tuba player Jon Sass since 1986. His most celebrated collaborations include several albums with American soul-blues singer Terry Evans -- "Visions" (2008), "Delta Time" (2012, featuring Ry Cooder) and the live album "True & Blue" (2015) -- as well as "Pay Day" (2021) with Big Daddy Wilson. Blues pianist Charles Brown recorded Theessink''s composition "Love Sweet Love" on his own 1998 album "Lifeline." In 2001 Theessink received Vienna''s Goldener Rathausmann award. He has released more than two dozen albums across his career, several of which reached the Austrian Top 40, with "Visions" (2008) peaking at number 8. He continues to record and tour into his late 70s, marking milestone "Birthday Bash" concert releases in 2009, 2014, 2019 and 2025.', 'Hans Theessink ble født 5. april 1948 i Enschede i Nederland, og har blitt en av Europas mest respekterte akustiske country-blues-artister (Kilde: de.wikipedia.org; en.wikipedia.org). Selvlært på gitar etter å ha hørt innspillinger med Big Bill Broonzy og Lead Belly tidlig på 1960-tallet, lærte han også mandolin og banjo, og startet opptredenskarrieren som gatemusiker med Silly Skiffle Group i Nederland og Tyskland. Etter en periode i Danmark, der han spilte inn debutalbumet «Next Morning at Sunrise» i 1970, flyttet han permanent til Wien i Østerrike i 1982, etter en konsert i 1979 der han møtte sin fremtidige kone Milica Djokic, som siden har vært hans manager gjennom deres eget selskap Blue Groove (Kilde: de.wikipedia.org). Theessinks musikk henter fra Delta-blues, folk, gospel, soul, Cajun, New Orleans-jazz og afrikanske tradisjoner, spilt nesten utelukkende på akustiske instrumenter uten digitale effekter. Siden 2004 har han turnert med Hans Theessink Band, og har jobbet tett med tubaspiller Jon Sass siden 1986. Hans mest kjente samarbeid inkluderer flere album med den amerikanske soul-blues-sangeren Terry Evans -- «Visions» (2008), «Delta Time» (2012, med Ry Cooder) og liveutgivelsen «True & Blue» (2015) -- samt «Pay Day» (2021) med Big Daddy Wilson. Bluespianisten Charles Brown spilte inn Theessinks komposisjon «Love Sweet Love» på sitt eget album «Lifeline» i 1998. I 2001 mottok Theessink Wiens Goldener Rathausmann-utmerkelse. Han har gitt ut over to dusin album gjennom karrieren, hvorav flere nådde den østerrikske Topp 40-listen, med «Visions» (2008) på sin beste 8. plass. Han fortsetter å spille inn og turnere godt inn i 70-årene, med jubileumskonsertutgivelser i 2009, 2014, 2019 og 2025.', 'Hans Theessink föddes den 5 april 1948 i Enschede i Nederländerna, och har blivit en av Europas mest respekterade akustiska country-blues-artister (Källa: de.wikipedia.org; en.wikipedia.org). Självlärd på gitarr efter att ha hört inspelningar med Big Bill Broonzy och Lead Belly i början av 1960-talet, lärde han sig även mandolin och banjo, och inledde sin uppträdandekarriär som gatumusikant med Silly Skiffle Group i Nederländerna och Tyskland. Efter en period i Danmark, där han spelade in debutalbumet "Next Morning at Sunrise" 1970, flyttade han permanent till Wien i Österrike 1982, efter en konsert 1979 där han träffade sin blivande hustru Milica Djokic, som sedan dess varit hans manager genom deras eget bolag Blue Groove (Källa: de.wikipedia.org). Theessinks musik hämtar från deltablues, folk, gospel, soul, Cajun, New Orleans-jazz och afrikanska traditioner, spelad nästan uteslutande på akustiska instrument utan digitala effekter. Sedan 2004 har han turnerat med Hans Theessink Band, och har arbetat nära med tubaisten Jon Sass sedan 1986. Hans mest kända samarbeten inkluderar flera album med den amerikanska soul-blues-sångaren Terry Evans -- "Visions" (2008), "Delta Time" (2012, med Ry Cooder) och livealbumet "True & Blue" (2015) -- samt "Pay Day" (2021) med Big Daddy Wilson. Bluespianisten Charles Brown spelade in Theessinks komposition "Love Sweet Love" på sitt eget album "Lifeline" 1998. År 2001 mottog Theessink Wiens Goldener Rathausmann-utmärkelse. Han har släppt över två dussin album under karriären, varav flera nådde den österrikiska Topp 40-listan, med "Visions" (2008) på sin bästa 8:e plats. Han fortsätter att spela in och turnera långt in i 70-årsåldern, med jubileumskonsertutgivningar 2009, 2014, 2019 och 2025.', 'Hans Theessink wurde am 5. April 1948 in Enschede, Niederlande, geboren und zählt zu Europas angesehensten Vertretern des akustischen Country-Blues (Quelle: de.wikipedia.org; en.wikipedia.org). Autodidaktisch an der Gitarre, nachdem er Anfang der 1960er-Jahre Aufnahmen von Big Bill Broonzy und Lead Belly gehört hatte, lernte er zudem Mandoline und Banjo und begann seine Auftrittslaufbahn als Straßenmusiker mit der Silly Skiffle Group in den Niederlanden und Deutschland. Nach einer Zeit in Dänemark, wo er 1970 sein Debütalbum „Next Morning at Sunrise" aufnahm, zog er 1982 dauerhaft nach Wien, Österreich, nachdem er 1979 bei einem Konzert seine spätere Frau Milica Djokic kennengelernt hatte, die seither über das gemeinsame Label und die Agentur Blue Groove sein Management führt (Quelle: de.wikipedia.org). Theessinks Musik schöpft aus Delta-Blues, Folk, Gospel, Soul, Cajun, New-Orleans-Jazz und afrikanischen Traditionen und wird fast ausschließlich auf akustischen Instrumenten ohne digitale Effekte gespielt. Seit 2004 tourt er mit der Hans Theessink Band und arbeitet seit 1986 eng mit dem Tubisten Jon Sass zusammen. Zu seinen bekanntesten Kollaborationen zählen mehrere Alben mit dem amerikanischen Soul-Blues-Sänger Terry Evans -- „Visions" (2008), „Delta Time" (2012, mit Ry Cooder) und das Live-Album „True & Blue" (2015) -- sowie „Pay Day" (2021) mit Big Daddy Wilson. Der Blues-Pianist Charles Brown nahm Theessinks Komposition „Love Sweet Love" auf seinem eigenen Album „Lifeline" von 1998 auf. 2001 erhielt Theessink den Wiener Goldenen Rathausmann. Er hat im Laufe seiner Karriere mehr als zwei Dutzend Alben veröffentlicht, mehrere davon in den österreichischen Top 40, mit „Visions" (2008) auf Platz 8 als bester Chartplatzierung. Er nimmt und tourt bis weit in seine 70er-Jahre hinein weiter, mit Jubiläumskonzert-Veröffentlichungen 2009, 2014, 2019 und 2025.', 'Hans Theessink urodził się 5 kwietnia 1948 roku w Enschede w Holandii i stał się jednym z najbardziej cenionych w Europie artystów akustycznego country bluesa (Źródło: de.wikipedia.org; en.wikipedia.org). Samouk na gitarze po usłyszeniu na początku lat 60. nagrań Big Billa Broonzy''ego i Lead Belly''ego, nauczył się także mandoliny i banjo, a swoją karierę koncertową rozpoczął jako muzyk uliczny z Silly Skiffle Group w Holandii i Niemczech. Po okresie spędzonym w Danii, gdzie nagrał swój debiutancki album „Next Morning at Sunrise" w 1970 roku, na stałe przeniósł się do Wiednia w Austrii w 1982 roku, po koncercie w 1979 roku, na którym poznał swoją przyszłą żonę Milicę Djokic, która od tego czasu zarządza jego karierą poprzez ich własną wytwórnię i agencję Blue Groove (Źródło: de.wikipedia.org). Muzyka Theessinka czerpie z bluesa Delty, folku, gospel, soulu, cajun, jazzu z Nowego Orleanu i tradycji afrykańskich, grana niemal wyłącznie na instrumentach akustycznych bez cyfrowych efektów. Od 2004 roku koncertuje z Hans Theessink Band, a od 1986 roku ściśle współpracuje z tubistą Jonem Sassem. Do jego najbardziej znanych współprac należy kilka albumów z amerykańskim wokalistą soul-bluesowym Terrym Evansem -- „Visions" (2008), „Delta Time" (2012, z udziałem Ry Coodera) i album koncertowy „True & Blue" (2015) -- a także „Pay Day" (2021) z Big Daddy Wilsonem. Pianista bluesowy Charles Brown nagrał kompozycję Theessinka „Love Sweet Love" na swoim własnym albumie „Lifeline" z 1998 roku. W 2001 roku Theessink otrzymał wiedeńską nagrodę Goldener Rathausmann. W ciągu swojej kariery wydał ponad dwa tuziny albumów, z których kilka trafiło na austriacką listę Top 40, przy czym „Visions" (2008) osiągnął najwyższą, 8. pozycję. Nadal nagrywa i koncertuje, mając blisko 80 lat, z jubileuszowymi wydawnictwami koncertowymi „Birthday Bash" w 2009, 2014, 2019 i 2025 roku.', '1948-04-05', NULL, NULL, 'Enschede, Nederland', 'Enschede, Nederland (bosatt i Wien, Østerrike)', '1970–nu', 'Hans Theessink is widely regarded as one of Europe''s most significant stylistic innovators of acoustic country-blues, drawing collaborators of the caliber of Ry Cooder and Charles Brown to his own compositions and building a career that has carried the Delta blues tradition to German-speaking audiences for over five decades (Source: de.wikipedia.org).', 'Hans Theessink regnes som en av Europas viktigste stilistiske fornyere av akustisk country-blues, og har trukket til seg samarbeidspartnere på nivå med Ry Cooder og Charles Brown, og bygget en karriere som har brakt Delta-bluestradisjonen til tysktalende publikum i over fem tiår (Kilde: de.wikipedia.org).', 'Hans Theessink betraktas som en av Europas viktigaste stilistiska förnyare av akustisk country-blues, och har dragit till sig samarbetspartners i klass med Ry Cooder och Charles Brown, och byggt en karriär som fört deltablues-traditionen till tysktalande publik i över fem decennier (Källa: de.wikipedia.org).', 'Hans Theessink gilt als einer der bedeutendsten stilistischen Erneuerer des akustischen Country-Blues in Europa, der Mitstreiter vom Format eines Ry Cooder und Charles Brown anzog und eine Karriere aufgebaut hat, die die Delta-Blues-Tradition seit über fünf Jahrzehnten einem deutschsprachigen Publikum nahebringt (Quelle: de.wikipedia.org).', 'Hans Theessink jest uważany za jednego z najważniejszych innowatorów stylistycznych akustycznego country bluesa w Europie, przyciągając współpracowników na poziomie Ry Coodera i Charlesa Browna, budując karierę, która od ponad pięciu dekad przybliża tradycję bluesa Delty niemieckojęzycznej publiczności (Źródło: de.wikipedia.org).', '[]', '{"no":[],"en":[],"sv":[],"de":[],"pl":[]}', '["Blue Groove","Ruf Records"]', '["Vocals","Guitar","Mandolin","Banjo"]', '["Delta Blues","Acoustic Blues","Roots Blues"]', '{"no":[{"relation":"Kone/manager","name":"Milica Djokic","note":"Gift 1979; har vært hans manager gjennom deres felles selskap Blue Groove siden de møttes på en konsert i 1979.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"en":[{"relation":"Wife/manager","name":"Milica Djokic","note":"Married in 1979; has managed his career through their shared label Blue Groove since they met at a concert in 1979.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"sv":[{"relation":"Fru/manager","name":"Milica Djokic","note":"Gift 1979; har varit hans manager genom deras gemensamma bolag Blue Groove sedan de träffades på en konsert 1979.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"de":[{"relation":"Ehefrau/Managerin","name":"Milica Djokic","note":"Heirat 1979; managt seine Karriere über das gemeinsame Label Blue Groove, seit sie sich 1979 bei einem Konzert kennenlernten.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"pl":[{"relation":"Żona/menedżerka","name":"Milica Djokic","note":"Ślub w 1979 roku; zarządza jego karierą poprzez wspólną wytwórnię Blue Groove od czasu, gdy poznali się na koncercie w 1979 roku.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}]}', '{"no":["Tidlig 1960-tallet: Selvlært gitar etter å ha hørt Big Bill Broonzy og Lead Belly (Kilde: de.wikipedia.org).","1970: Debutalbumet «Next Morning at Sunrise» spilt inn i Danmark.","1979: Møtte sin fremtidige kone Milica Djokic på en konsert.","1982: Flyttet permanent til Wien, Østerrike.","1986: Startet samarbeid med tubaspiller Jon Sass.","2001: Mottok Wiens Goldener Rathausmann-utmerkelse.","2004: Begynte å turnere med Hans Theessink Band."],"en":["Early 1960s: Self-taught guitar after hearing Big Bill Broonzy and Lead Belly (Source: de.wikipedia.org).","1970: Debut album \"Next Morning at Sunrise\" recorded in Denmark.","1979: Met future wife Milica Djokic at a concert.","1982: Relocated permanently to Vienna, Austria.","1986: Began collaboration with tuba player Jon Sass.","2001: Received Vienna''s Goldener Rathausmann award.","2004: Began touring with the Hans Theessink Band."],"sv":["Tidigt 1960-tal: Självlärd gitarr efter att ha hört Big Bill Broonzy och Lead Belly (Källa: de.wikipedia.org).","1970: Debutalbumet \"Next Morning at Sunrise\" spelades in i Danmark.","1979: Träffade sin blivande hustru Milica Djokic på en konsert.","1982: Flyttade permanent till Wien, Österrike.","1986: Inledde samarbete med tubaisten Jon Sass.","2001: Mottog Wiens Goldener Rathausmann-utmärkelse.","2004: Började turnera med Hans Theessink Band."],"de":["Frühe 1960er-Jahre: Autodidaktisches Gitarrenspiel nach dem Hören von Big Bill Broonzy und Lead Belly (Quelle: de.wikipedia.org).","1970: Debütalbum „Next Morning at Sunrise\" in Dänemark aufgenommen.","1979: Lernt seine spätere Frau Milica Djokic bei einem Konzert kennen.","1982: Dauerhafter Umzug nach Wien, Österreich.","1986: Beginn der Zusammenarbeit mit Tubist Jon Sass.","2001: Erhält den Wiener Goldenen Rathausmann.","2004: Beginnt Touren mit der Hans Theessink Band."],"pl":["Wczesne lata 60.: Samouk gitary po usłyszeniu Big Billa Broonzy''ego i Lead Belly''ego (Źródło: de.wikipedia.org).","1970: Nagranie debiutanckiego albumu \"Next Morning at Sunrise\" w Danii.","1979: Poznanie przyszłej żony Milicy Djokic na koncercie.","1982: Przeprowadzka na stałe do Wiednia w Austrii.","1986: Rozpoczęcie współpracy z tubistą Jonem Sassem.","2001: Otrzymanie wiedeńskiej nagrody Goldener Rathausmann.","2004: Rozpoczęcie tras koncertowych z Hans Theessink Band."]}', '{"no":[{"category":"Gitar","name":"Akustisk gitar (Hans Theessink)","note":"Selvlært, inspirert av Big Bill Broonzy og Lead Belly.","years":null},{"category":"Annet","name":"Mandolin og banjo","note":null,"years":null}],"en":[{"category":"Gitar","name":"Acoustic guitar (Hans Theessink)","note":"Self-taught, inspired by Big Bill Broonzy and Lead Belly.","years":null},{"category":"Annet","name":"Mandolin and banjo","note":null,"years":null}],"sv":[{"category":"Gitar","name":"Akustisk gitarr (Hans Theessink)","note":"Självlärd, inspirerad av Big Bill Broonzy och Lead Belly.","years":null},{"category":"Annet","name":"Mandolin och banjo","note":null,"years":null}],"de":[{"category":"Gitar","name":"Akustikgitarre (Hans Theessink)","note":"Autodidakt, inspiriert von Big Bill Broonzy und Lead Belly.","years":null},{"category":"Annet","name":"Mandoline und Banjo","note":null,"years":null}],"pl":[{"category":"Gitar","name":"Gitara akustyczna (Hans Theessink)","note":"Samouk, inspirowany Big Billem Broonzym i Lead Bellym.","years":null},{"category":"Annet","name":"Mandolina i banjo","note":null,"years":null}]}', '{"no":[],"en":[],"sv":[],"de":[],"pl":[]}', '{"no":[{"name":"Terry Evans","note":"Flere samarbeidsalbum: «Visions» (2008), «Delta Time» (2012) og liveutgivelsen «True & Blue» (2015).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Ry Cooder","note":"Gjesteopptreden på «Delta Time» (2012).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Charles Brown","note":"Spilte inn Theessinks komposisjon «Love Sweet Love» på albumet «Lifeline» (1998).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Big Daddy Wilson","note":"Samarbeidsalbumet «Pay Day» (2021).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Jon Sass","note":"Tubaspiller, fast samarbeidspartner siden 1986.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"en":[{"name":"Terry Evans","note":"Several collaborative albums: \"Visions\" (2008), \"Delta Time\" (2012) and the live album \"True & Blue\" (2015).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Ry Cooder","note":"Guest appearance on \"Delta Time\" (2012).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Charles Brown","note":"Recorded Theessink''s composition \"Love Sweet Love\" on the album \"Lifeline\" (1998).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Big Daddy Wilson","note":"Collaborative album \"Pay Day\" (2021).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Jon Sass","note":"Tuba player, regular collaborator since 1986.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"sv":[{"name":"Terry Evans","note":"Flera samarbetsalbum: \"Visions\" (2008), \"Delta Time\" (2012) och livealbumet \"True & Blue\" (2015).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Ry Cooder","note":"Gästmedverkan på \"Delta Time\" (2012).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Charles Brown","note":"Spelade in Theessinks komposition \"Love Sweet Love\" på albumet \"Lifeline\" (1998).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Big Daddy Wilson","note":"Samarbetsalbumet \"Pay Day\" (2021).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Jon Sass","note":"Tubaist, återkommande samarbetspartner sedan 1986.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"de":[{"name":"Terry Evans","note":"Mehrere gemeinsame Alben: „Visions\" (2008), „Delta Time\" (2012) und das Live-Album „True & Blue\" (2015).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Ry Cooder","note":"Gastauftritt auf „Delta Time\" (2012).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Charles Brown","note":"Nahm Theessinks Komposition „Love Sweet Love\" auf dem Album „Lifeline\" (1998) auf.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Big Daddy Wilson","note":"Gemeinsames Album „Pay Day\" (2021).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Jon Sass","note":"Tubist, regelmäßiger Mitstreiter seit 1986.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}],"pl":[{"name":"Terry Evans","note":"Kilka wspólnych albumów: \"Visions\" (2008), \"Delta Time\" (2012) i album koncertowy \"True & Blue\" (2015).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Ry Cooder","note":"Gościnny udział na \"Delta Time\" (2012).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Charles Brown","note":"Nagrał kompozycję Theessinka \"Love Sweet Love\" na albumie \"Lifeline\" (1998).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Big Daddy Wilson","note":"Wspólny album \"Pay Day\" (2021).","source":"de.wikipedia.org"},{"name":"Jon Sass","note":"Tubista, stały współpracownik od 1986 roku.","source":"de.wikipedia.org"}]}', '[{"kind":"featured","title":"I''m A Man - Bo Diddley, Hans Theessink, Ron Wood, Jazzfest Wiesen, Austria, 1988.07.08","youtube_id":"P951k311Cek","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"featured","title":"\"Polk Salad Annie\" - Tony Joe White and special guest Hans Theessink. Vienna Oct.25th 2002","youtube_id":"xECo-emMYnI","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"Hans Theessink Band DK Tonder Festival Aug.2025","youtube_id":"pUBWb2fzzZQ","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"Hans Theessink Band Stadtsaal Vienna Sa.7.6.25","youtube_id":"G9K4P4xiU5Y","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"Maybellene - Hans Theessink solo @ Stadthalle Vienna, Elvis Presley Festival Oct.25th 2002","youtube_id":"fGLH3V4CKT8","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"The Planet - Hans Theessink SOLO - Live on TV","youtube_id":"Pdh_TNefhWE","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"HANS THEESSINK & USTAD NOOR BAKHSH play \"Shahbaz Qalandar\"","youtube_id":"UUvQzYnz-3M","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"Hans Theessink & Wilfried - Sittin'' On Top Of The World, 1998","youtube_id":"xwWRXqF0E1Q","channel":"Hans Theessink"},{"kind":"more","title":"SAINT JAMES INFIRMARY - Hans Theessink & Knud Møller","youtube_